[Article 22 of the Farmland Act (Prevention of Fragmentation of Farmland Ownership)] [MT]
(1) The State and local governments may provide necessary support to prevent the fragmentation of farmland ownership by farmers or agricultural corporations, so that farmland may be inherited, gifted, or transferred in bulk to one farmer or to a single agricultural corporation.
(2) Farmland on which an agricultural production base maintenance project under the Act on the Improvement of Agricultural and Fishing Villages has been implemented shall not be divided except in any of the following cases:
(1) Dividing farmland included in a residential area, commercial area, or industrial area of an urban district, or in land for urban or county planning facilities, under the National Land Planning and Utilization Act;
(2) Dividing farmland that has been converted after obtaining permission for farmland conversion pursuant to Article 34(1) (including authorizations, permits, approvals, etc., under other statutes that are deemed to be permission for farmland conversion) or after filing a farmland conversion notification pursuant to Article 35 or Article 43;
(3) Dividing so that the area of each parcel after division exceeds 2,000 square meters;
(4) Dividing for reasons specified by Presidential Decree, such as improvement of farmland, exchange or consolidation of farmland.
