[Article 62 of the Farmland Act (Penalty Provision for Corporations and Others)] [MT]
Where the representative of a corporation or an agent, employee, or other worker of a corporation or individual, in relation to the business of that corporation or individual, commits a violation corresponding to any of Articles 57 through 61, in addition to punishing the actor, the corporation or individual shall also be imposed the fine prescribed in the relevant provision. However, this shall not apply where the corporation or individual has not neglected to exercise reasonable care and supervision with respect to the relevant business in order to prevent such violation.

[Article 60 of the Farmland Act (Penal Provisions)] [MT]
Any person who falls under any of the following subparagraphs shall be punished by imprisonment for not more than three years or by a fine not exceeding 30,000,000 won:
(1) A person who has violated the prohibited acts under Article 7-2;
(2) A person who has converted farmland without filing the notification under Article 35 or Article 43;
(3) A person who has used farmland for other purposes without filing the temporary use notification for other purposes of farmland under Article 36-2(1);
(4) A person who has improved farmland without complying with the farmland improvement standards under Article 41-2;
(5) A person who has carried out embankment or excavation of farmland without filing the notification or change notification under Article 41-3(1).

[Article 105 of the Civil Act (Default Rule)]
Where the parties to a legal act express an intention different from a provision of law that is not related to good morals or other public order, their intention shall prevail.

[Article 9 of the National Tax Collection Act [MT] (Collection before the due date)] The head of the competent tax office may, even before the payment due date, collect national taxes for which the tax liability has already been determined, where the taxpayer falls under any of the following subparagraphs:

(1) where compulsory collection or other measures for disposition of arrears have been commenced due to delinquency in payment of national taxes, local taxes or public charges;
(2) where an auction for the purpose of compulsory execution or enforcement of security rights under the Civil Execution Act [MT] has been commenced, or where a declaration of bankruptcy has been made under the Debtor Rehabilitation and Bankruptcy Act [MT];
(3) where the taxpayer has been subjected to an order suspending dealings by a clearinghouse for bills pursuant to the Bills of Exchange Act [MT] or the Cheque Act [MT];
(4) where a corporation has been dissolved;
(5) where it is recognized that there is an act intended to evade national taxes;
(6) where the taxpayer has not appointed a tax agent and does not have an address or place of residence in the Republic of Korea.

[Article 126 of the Civil Procedure Act (Change of Security)] The court may, upon the application of the provider of security, by decision order that the security deposited be changed. However, where a party applies to substitute, pursuant to a contract, the security deposited with another security, the court shall comply with such application.

[Article 106 of the Local Tax Act [MT] (Evaluation of Suitability of Land Subject to Separate Taxation, etc.)] The Minister of the Interior and Safety may, when intending to reduce or reorganize the land subject to separate taxation under Article 106(1)(3) or when intending to expand or add land subject to separate taxation (hereinafter in this Article referred to as "land subject to separate taxation"), comprehensively consider the purpose of separate taxation, tax equity, the financial circumstances of local governments, and whether there is overlap with other support measures, and evaluate the appropriateness of separate taxation.

[Article 9 of the Local Tax Act [MT] (Tax Exemptions)] Acquisition tax shall not be imposed on acquisitions by the State or local governments (excluding corporations that are deemed to be the State or local governments under other statutes; the same shall apply hereinafter), unions of local governments pursuant to Article 176(1) of the Local Autonomy Act [MT] (hereinafter "unions of local governments"), foreign governments and international organizations in the Republic of Korea. However, acquisition tax shall be imposed on acquisitions by foreign governments that tax acquisitions by agencies of the Government of the Republic of Korea.

[Article 9 of the Local Tax Act [MT] (Tax Exemptions)] Real estate acquired on condition that it will vest in or be donated/ceded to the State, local governments or unions of local governments (including cases where it vests in the manner provided for in Article 4(3) of the Act on Private Investment in Infrastructure [MT]; hereinafter in this paragraph referred to as "vesting, etc."), and infrastructure corresponding to each subparagraph of Article 2(1) of the Act on Private Investment in Infrastructure [MT], shall not be subject to acquisition tax. However, in any of the following cases, acquisition tax shall be imposed on the relevant portion. <Amended Dec. 27, 2010; July 24, 2015; Dec. 29, 2015>

(1) Where the property is sold or donated to a third party without performing the condition of vesting, etc., or where the condition is changed so that vesting, etc. is not performed;
(2) Where, as consideration for vesting, etc., the acquirer receives gratuitous transfer of real estate and infrastructure owned by the State, etc., or is granted a gratuitous right to use the object subject to donation.

[Article 126 of the Local Tax Act [MT] (Tax Exemptions)] Automobile tax shall not be imposed on the owners of any of the following motor vehicles:

(1) Motor vehicles provided by the State or local governments for national defense, security, policing, traffic patrol or firefighting;
(2) Motor vehicles provided by the State or local governments for patient transport, cleaning, refuse removal or road works;
(3) Other motor vehicles used by diplomatic missions in the Republic of Korea and other motor vehicles as prescribed by Presidential Decree.

[Article 26 of the Local Tax Act [MT] (Tax Exemptions)] Registration and license tax shall not be imposed on registrations or licenses received by the State, local governments, unions of local governments, foreign governments and international organizations in the Republic of Korea for themselves. However, registration and license tax shall be imposed on registrations or licenses of foreign governments that tax registrations or licenses of agencies of the Government of the Republic of Korea.

[Article 26 of the Local Tax Act [MT] (Tax Exemptions)] Registration and license tax shall not be imposed on any of the following registrations, registrations or licenses. <Amended Dec. 29, 2015; Dec. 29, 2023>

(1) Registrations or recordings pursuant to Article 6(3), Article 25(1) through (3), Article 26(1), Article 26(3), Article 27, Article 76(4), Article 362(3), Article 578-5(3), Article 578-8(3) and Article 578-9(3) of the Debtor Rehabilitation and Bankruptcy Act [MT];
(2) Registrations or recordings arising from changes in administrative district, changes in resident registration number, changes of lot number by the competent cadastral authority, changes in units of measure, errors by the registration or recording officer, and similar causes, which are simple corrections, restorations or amendment registrations or recordings of address, name, resident registration number, lot number, unit of measure, etc.;
(3) Other registrations prescribed by Presidential Decree, such as registrations of land the land-category of which is "graveyard";
(4) Licenses prescribed by Presidential Decree for which taxation by registration and license tax is not appropriate, such as simple changes in notation of the license.

