[Article 3 of the Act on the Improvement of Urban Areas and Residential Environments (Basic Policy on Urban and Residential Environment Improvement)] The Minister of Land, Infrastructure and Transport shall, every ten years, establish basic policies including the following matters to improve urban and residential environments, and shall review their validity every five years and reflect the results in the basic policies.

(1) National policy directions for urban and residential environment improvement;
(2) Direction for the formulation of the basic plan for urban and residential environment improvement pursuant to Article 4(1);
(3) Surveys of old and substandard residential areas and the formulation of improvement plans;
(4) Financial support plans necessary for urban and residential environment improvement;
(5) Other matters necessary for urban and residential environment improvement as prescribed by Presidential Decree.

Chapter 2 Formulation of the Basic Plan and Designation of Maintenance Areas

[Article 4 of the Act on the Improvement of Urban Areas and Residential Environments (Formulation of the Basic Plan for Urban and Residential Environment Improvement)] The Mayor of a Special City, the Mayor of a Metropolitan City, the Mayor of a Special Self-Governing City, the Governor of a Special Self-Governing Province or the Mayor of a City shall formulate a basic plan for urban and residential environment improvement (hereinafter the "basic plan") for their jurisdiction every ten years. However, a provincial governor may omit formulating a basic plan for a city that is not a metropolitan city if the governor determines that there is no need to formulate such a plan.

[Article 6 of the Act on the Improvement of Urban Areas and Residential Environments (Hearing of Residents' Opinions for Formulation of the Basic Plan, etc.)] (1) When the authority competent to formulate the basic plan intends to formulate or amend the basic plan, it shall make the plan available for public inspection by residents for at least 14 days and solicit their opinions, and if the opinions presented are deemed reasonable, it shall reflect them in the basic plan.

(2) The authority competent to formulate the basic plan shall, together with the public inspection under paragraph (1), solicit the opinion of the local council. In this case, the local council shall present its opinion within 60 days from the date on which the authority competent to formulate the basic plan notifies the basic plan; if 60 days pass without presenting an opinion, it shall be deemed that there is no objection.

(3) Notwithstanding paragraphs (1) and (2), when changing minor matters prescribed by Presidential Decree, the procedures of public inspection by residents and solicitation of the local council's opinion may be omitted.

[Article 8 of the Act on the Improvement of Urban Areas and Residential Environments (Designation of Maintenance Areas)] The authority competent to designate maintenance areas may, when necessary for the construction of access roads to a maintenance area, designate the maintenance area to include the access road area and its adjacent area.

[Article 28 of the Act on the Improvement of Urban Areas and Residential Environments (Project Implementer for Redevelopment and Reconstruction Projects)] Where any of the following applies, the Mayor, County Governor, etc. may, on behalf of the relevant association or the land, etc. owners, directly implement the maintenance project or have the Korea Land and Housing Corporation, etc. or a designated developer implement the maintenance project on behalf of the relevant association or the land, etc. owners:

(1) Where the maintenance project has been delayed for a long time or it is recognized that it is difficult for the relevant association or the land, etc. owners to continue to pursue the maintenance project due to disputes concerning rights relationships;
(2) Where requested with the consent of a majority of the land, etc. owners (in the case of establishing an association, the members of the association).

[Article 64 of the Act on the Improvement of Urban Areas and Residential Environments (Right to Request Sale in Reconstruction Projects)] The project implementer of a reconstruction project shall, within 30 days from the date on which the authorization for the project implementation plan is announced, urge in writing the following persons to respond as to whether they agree to the establishment of the association or to the designation of the project implementer:

(1) Persons who did not agree to the establishment of the association under Article 35(3) through (5);
(2) Persons who did not agree to the designation of the project implementer as the Mayor, County Governor, etc., the Korea Land and Housing Corporation, etc., or a trust company under Article 26(1) and Article 27(1).

[Article 65 of the Act on the Improvement of Urban Areas and Residential Environments (Application of the Act on the Acquisition and Compensation of Land, etc. for Public Projects)] When applying the Act on the Acquisition and Compensation of Land, etc. for Public Projects [MT] pursuant to paragraph (1), at the time when the authorization for the project implementation plan is announced (in the case where the Mayor, County Governor, etc. directly implements the maintenance project, this means the public announcement of the project implementation plan pursuant to Article 50(9); the same shall apply hereinafter in this Article), it shall be deemed that the project recognition and its public announcement under Article 20(1) and Article 22(1) of the same Act have been made.

[Article 19 of the Act on the Improvement of Urban Areas and Residential Environments (Restrictions on Acts, etc.)] Notwithstanding paragraph (1), any of the following acts may be carried out without obtaining permission:

(1) acts for emergency measures necessary for disaster recovery or disaster response;
(2) where there is a concern about safety accidents such as the collapse of an existing building, acts for safety measures for the relevant building;
(3) other acts prescribed by Presidential Decree.

[Article 25 of the Act on the Improvement of Urban Areas and Residential Environments (Implementer of Redevelopment and Reconstruction Projects)]
Reconstruction projects shall be implemented by an association, or the association may, with the consent of a majority of the association members, implement them jointly with the mayor, the county governor, the Korea Land & Housing Corporation, constructors, or a registered project operator.

[Article 27 of the Act on the Improvement of Urban Areas and Residential Environments (Designated Developer for Redevelopment and Reconstruction Projects)]
The mayor, the county governor, etc. may, when a redevelopment project or a reconstruction project falls under any of the following subparagraphs, designate as the project implementer a land owner, a public‑private joint corporation as referred to in Article 2(12) of the Act on Private Investment in Infrastructure [MT], or a trust business operator who meets the requirements prescribed by Presidential Decree (hereinafter referred to as the "designated developer") and have the maintenance project implemented by such person. <Amended June 12, 2018>

(1) when it is recognized that, due to a natural disaster, a restriction on use or prohibition of use under Article 27 of the Framework Act on the Management of Disasters and Safety [MT] or Article 23 of the Special Act on the Safety and Maintenance of Facilities [MT], or other unavoidable reasons, there is an urgent need to carry out the maintenance project;

(2) when an application for approval of the project implementation plan is not filed within two years from the scheduled date of implementation of the maintenance project set forth in the maintenance plan notified pursuant to the preamble of Article 16(2), or when the contents of the application for approval of the project implementation plan are recognized as illegal or unjust (except in the case of reconstruction projects);

